    TEST-0001: run the BookingStore contract against the real JSON file
    
    bookingStoreContract() is what every BookingStore promises, written
    once. FakeBookingStore already passed it, and that's why the core's
    unit tests can trust the fake. One line runs the same contract against
    a JsonBookingStore on a real file in a temporary directory. That's an
    integration test: one real adapter, its real resource, and no core.
    
    The contract failed on its first run. A JsonBookingStore whose file
    doesn't exist yet threw ENOENT instead of having no bookings, so the
    first booking on a new machine would have crashed. The fake can't have
    that bug, and no core test could see it. The adapter now treats a
    missing file as no bookings.

diff --git a/src/adapters/JsonBookingStore.ts b/src/adapters/JsonBookingStore.ts
index 6a693ef..cdf85db 100644
--- a/src/adapters/JsonBookingStore.ts
+++ b/src/adapters/JsonBookingStore.ts
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@ export class JsonBookingStore implements BookingStore {
 	}
 
 	private readAll(): Booking[] {
+		// nothing has been booked yet
+		if (!fs.existsSync(this.file)) {
+			return [];
+		}
 		return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(this.file, "utf8")).bookings;
 	}
 }
